  "_comment": "E13 edge-ablation (#464 follow-up, write-time-structure question, 2026-06-21). Non-destructive client-side ablation (does NOT mutate the shared live data graph): remove fraction p of related edges, measure GOLD REACHABILITY@hops2 from top-3 SEARCH seeds = ceiling on context-pack coverage. RESULT: connectedness CAUSALLY enables multi-hop retrieval. Gold reachability falls monotonically with edge removal (1.0 -> 0.38 at 90% removed). KEY: BRIDGE gold (>=2 hops from seed, the multi-hop payload) degrades 5-10x FASTER than NEAR gold (<=1 hop, which search-only also gets): at 40% removed bridge=0.66 vs near=0.96; at 50% bridge=0.47 vs near=0.91; at 80% bridge=0.09 vs near=0.58. So the related edges are exactly what make the bridge nodes reachable -> the entire context-pack multi-hop advantage is downstream of write-time edge quality. NUANCE: graceful at low ablation (10% removed -> bridge still 0.95) = redundant connectivity; you do not need every edge, you need the BRIDGE edges (cross-region links). Skill guidance: author the connective tissue (bridge nodes + cross-cluster related edges), for FIDELITY; do not over-connect."
